  "Question": "The ratio of Mary’s age to Alice’s age is \\(3 : 5.\\) Alice is \\(30\\) years old. How many years old is Mary?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(15\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(50\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The ratio \\(3:5\\) means Mary's age consists of three equal parts while Alice's consists of five of the same parts. Since Alice is \\(30\\), each part represents \\(30\\div5=6\\) years. Mary's age is therefore\n\\[\n3\\times6=18\\text{ years}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{18}\\), choice B.",
